Project A (C++ / armadillo)
===========================

* calculate the local density of a nuclear system

-> use git, doxygen, make, cxxtest, remark.js, quadratures, mandatory unit tests

1. prepare the project tree
2. implement the basis truncation (mandatory tests)
3. implement the basis functions calculation (mandatory tests)
6. implement the local density calculation (mandatory tests)
7. calculate and plot the local density (2D)
8. optimize the local density calculation
9. present your project

* introduction
* project presentation
* git
* zen of C++
* make
* Armadillo
* Doxygen
* CxxTest
* sum optimization
* valgrind
* gdb
* POVray
* latex
* markdown

Project B (Swig / Python)
=========================

* calculate some observables in Python

-> use swig to generate Python bindings
-> use project A from Python to calculate observables
-> for the rest of the project, use gitlab PRs only (only one project member with rw) !

1. generate the Python bindings of the project A
2. check the orthonormality of the basis states (basis overlap) using quadratures
3. implement the observables calculation A, Z, <Q20t>...
4. BONUS: implement the exact observables calculation (using HO representation of the operators)

* python
* venv/pip
* numpy
* python and C++
* swig
* matplotlib
* quadratures
